  "narrative": {
    "intro": "L3HARRIS Technologies has $354M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. L3HARRIS Technologies won 188 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.9M, and obligations are up 26.8% year over year. Annual obligations have varied: FY21 was $436M, FY22 was $480M, FY23 was $543M, FY24 was $492M, and FY25 was $279M. The Department of Transportation is the largest buyer in FY2026 to date at $172M, followed by the Department of Defense at $125M and the Department of Commerce at $54.9M. Engineering Services is the largest market this fiscal year at $148M, followed by Custom Computer Programming Services at $66.3M and Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $62.1M. Other notable markets include Satellite Telecommunications at $23.4M and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $16.9M. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity.",
    "sections": [
